-- title:
--   Points over the closed point specialise from a branch
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly over $L$, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), taken nonzero. Write $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the morphism obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$ along their common overlap. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$ and $X_k$ the fibre product of $X$ with $\operatorname{Spec}k$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, with its projection to $\operatorname{Spec}k$. Let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with $C_1,C_2$ integral schemes, and let $i_1,i_2$ be closed immersions $C_1\to X_k$, $C_2\to X_k$ commuting with the structure maps to $\operatorname{Spec}k$, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced, and its number of points equals some $n>0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating its maximal ideal, $\rho_O:A\to O$ an injective ring map, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa:O\to k$ a ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ the structure map $A\to k$. Let $X_O$ be the fibre product of $X$ with $\operatorname{Spec}O$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and $\mathrm{bc}:X_k\to X_O$ a morphism compatible with the first projections and with the second projections via $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Then for every point $y$ of $X_O$ whose image in $\operatorname{Spec}O$ does not lie in the basic open set $D(\varpi)$, the image of the generic point of $C_1$ under $i_1$ followed by $\mathrm{bc}$ specialises to $y$, or the image of the generic point of $C_2$ under $i_2$ followed by $\mathrm{bc}$ does.
--
--   This is the statement that, over the closed point of the coefficient ring $O$, every point of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ base-changed to $O$ lies in the closure of one of the two branches of the geometric special fibre. It feeds the construction of oriented étale crossing charts for this model and the resulting bound on the Krull dimension of its local rings.
